# ThermoSave Design System

Before changing or adding UI, read and follow **[`design.md`](../../design.md)** at the repo root. It is the source of truth for brand, color, type, section rhythm, CTAs, and nav chrome.

## Non-negotiables

1. **Industrial heat look** — charcoal ink (`#0c1014`), heat accent (`#c45c1a` / `#f0a060`). No SaaS purple, no Inter-default stacks, no cream+terracotta lifestyle look.
2. **Fonts** — Archivo (`--font-display`) for brand/headings; IBM Plex Sans for body.
3. **Primary CTAs** — heat fill `#c45c1a`, not default blue `--primary`, on marketing and global nav.
4. **Nav** — dark chrome that integrates with heroes (transparent over homepage / products·industries·clients collection + industry/client detail heroes at top; solid dark when scrolled / on light interiors e.g. product PDPs). Include Clientele in nav. Never a solid white bar over the dark hero.
5. **Tone** — engineer-to-engineer; numbers over hype; CTAs are assessment / call / WhatsApp. Follow **Hormozi value equation + Brunson Hook→Story→Offer** in `design.md` §1b. For Pakistan industry pages: **story splits (photo + short copy) after hero, then Mux/gallery dump**; never text-only PAS; videos sit in the same tile grid as photos. Clientele pages prove with named plants + Mux.
6. **Reuse** — prefer `components/landing/*`, `components/products/*`, `components/industries/*`, `components/clients/*`, and `components/landing/constants.ts` over duplicating patterns.
7. **Research online** — before writing or expanding an industry/process page, search current process + heat-loss + jacket data online; compress into short plant copy and stats. See `design.md` §1c and `AGENTS.md`.

If a change conflicts with `design.md`, update the implementation to match the doc — or update `design.md` deliberately when introducing a new standard.
